Preamble

This License is designed to provide a framework for making software and other types of works available in source code form while strictly prohibiting commercial exploitation. Unlike open source licenses that permit commercial use, this License grants permission for any form of non-commercial use—including running, copying, modifying, distributing, and combining—but strictly prohibits any use for profit-making purposes.

We believe that knowledge should flow freely, yet the fruits of creators' labor should not be exploited commercially without compensation. This License is designed to achieve this dual objective.



Section 1. Definitions

1.1 "This License" refers to the Non-Commercial Free Use License, Version 1.0.

1.2 "The Software" refers to all source code, object code, resource files, configuration documents, interface definitions, and related documentation materials accompanying this License, regardless of the medium of storage or presentation.

1.3 "Derivative Work" refers to any work, in whole or in part, created by modifying, translating, adapting, refactoring, extending, reverse engineering, or otherwise engaging in any form of secondary creation based upon the Software, regardless of whether such modification substantially alters the functionality or structure of the Software.

1.4 "Licensee" refers to any natural person, legal entity, or unincorporated organization that has lawfully obtained the Software and is bound by this License.

1.5 "Commercial Profit-Making Activity" refers to any form of use, copying, distribution, hosting, operation, or commercial exploitation of the Software or its Derivative Works for the purpose of directly or indirectly obtaining money, digital currency, goods, service compensation, equity options, advertising revenue, sponsorship donations, traffic monetization, or any other form of economic benefit.

1.6 "Hosted Service" refers to the provision of the functionality, interfaces, computing power, or data processing services of the Software or its Derivative Works to third parties through any computer network, regardless of the form in which such service is presented.



Section 2. Basic Permissions

Subject to the Licensee's strict and continued compliance with all terms and conditions of this License, this License grants the Licensee a worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable (except as terminated under Section 6), non-exclusive license to exercise the following rights:

2.1 Right to Run. The Licensee has the right to run the Software or its Derivative Works for any non-commercial purpose.

2.2 Right to Read. The Licensee has the right to read, view, and browse the source code and documentation of the Software.

2.3 Right to Copy and Distribute. The Licensee has the right to copy the Software or its Derivative Works and distribute them to any third party, provided that all copyright notices, author attributions, and the full text of this License contained in the Software are retained intact in their entirety.

2.4 Right to Modify and Create Derivatives. The Licensee has the right to make any modifications to the Software to produce Derivative Works, provided that such Derivative Works satisfy all of the following conditions:

(a) They must be made available to the public under the identical terms of this License;

(b) They must retain the original author's attribution and copyright notice in their entirety;

(c) They must clearly indicate in their documentation the modifications made and the date of such modifications.

2.5 Right to Combine and Integrate. The Licensee has the right to combine or integrate the Software or its Derivative Works with other software projects, provided that the original code portions of the Software remain subject to this License.



Section 3. Absolutely Prohibited Commercial Profit-Making Activities

Notwithstanding the broad permissions granted in Section 2, the Licensee is strictly prohibited from using the Software or its Derivative Works for any form of Commercial Profit-Making Activity. The scope of this prohibition includes, but is not limited to:

3.1 Prohibition on Direct Sale. The Licensee shall not sell, lease, resell, license, or distribute the Software or its Derivative Works in exchange for any form of consideration.

3.2 Prohibition on Commercial Hosted Services. The Licensee shall not provide the Software or its Derivative Works as a Hosted Service to any third party, directly or indirectly charging fees or obtaining other commercial benefits.

3.3 Prohibition on Embedding in Commercial Products. The Licensee shall not embed, integrate, or deploy the Software or its Derivative Works into any product, service, application, or business process that generates revenue. For the avoidance of doubt, even if the Software is used internally within a commercial organization, such use falls within the scope of this prohibition if it directly or indirectly supports the organization's commercial operations or revenue generation.

3.4 Prohibition on Commercialized Secondary Development. The Licensee shall not utilize the Software or its Derivative Works to provide technical consulting, custom development, or system integration services to any commercial entity in exchange for compensation.

3.5 Prohibition on Advertising and Traffic Monetization. The Licensee shall not utilize the Software or its Derivative Works to build websites, applications, or platforms through which revenue is generated by means of advertising placement, traffic direction, membership fees, virtual goods trading, or similar methods.

3.6 Prohibition on Circumvention. The Licensee shall not take any measures to circumvent, bypass, or undermine the use restrictions set forth in this License, including but not limited to indirectly engaging in the prohibited activities set forth in this Section through the establishment of affiliated entities, delegation to third parties, or segmentation of business processes.



